EXT. LEVIATHAN BACK MARKET - DAWN

A sleeping sea-beast the size of an island. Stalls on its spine. Rigging lashed to ribs. The skin breathes slowly.

YARROW (20s, sea-glass eyes, ragged oilskin) crouches by a stall of bottled winds.

CINDERMAE (70s, silver teeth, coal-black shawl) presides behind the counter.

BRISK (teen, gull on his shoulder) scrambles up a rope ladder. Out of breath.

SEUN (40s, copper armor, spear of whalebone) lurks at the edge, watching.

BRISK
Yarrow! They're coming!

YARROW
Who?

BRISK
The tide-wardens!

CINDERMAE
Quiet, boy. You'll wake the beast.

The leviathan's skin ripples. Stalls shudder. Bottles clink.

YARROW
How many?

BRISK
Six. Maybe seven.

SEUN
Eight.

They turn. Seun steps forward, spear lowered.

SEUN (CONT'D)
And I am the first.

CINDERMAE
Seun. You were a friend of this market.

SEUN
I was a friend of the market. The sea-king is the market's master.

YARROW
You swore an oath to the wind.

CINDERMAE
She swore an oath to the wind.

YARROW ^
She swore an oath to the wind.

SEUN
Oaths bend.

BRISK
(whispering)
The gull says run.

Seun hurls the spear. It bursts a jar of tempest. Wind howls out. The leviathan groans awake. The whole market tilts.

YARROW
Hold on!

Everyone grabs rope.
